     "<p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">I have the following model in SEM in JASP (which uses lavaan):</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 14px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">L ~ D</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 14px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">D ~ Q</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 14px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">Q ~ M</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 14px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">M ~ P</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 14px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">P ~ I   </p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 14px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">I ~ A    </p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 14px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">A ~ M</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 14px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">All these variables linearly interrelate. They&#39;re logged variables to make this so. </p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 14px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">I didn&#39;t standardize the data before estimation, and I&#39;m using the UNstandardized regression coefficients output of this model to predict output from input, in R, using the following R code:</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 14px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">------------------------------</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 14px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">x=USER SPECIFIED</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 14px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">x=log10(x)  # log the input </p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 14px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">x=x*-0.375</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 14px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">x=x*-0.875</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 14px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">x=x*-0.617</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 14px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">x=x*1.174</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 14px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">x=x*0.661</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 14px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">x=x*0.971</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 14px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">x=x*-0.947</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 14px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">x=10^(x)  # de-log the output</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 14px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">x</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 14px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">---------------------------------</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 14px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">The problem is I&#39;m not getting output within the expected range (and I do de-log the output. And the inputs tested are within the range of data of the model). Are the regression coefficients useable in this way? Or is what I&#39;m trying to do just non-sensical? <br>Might the problem be that the equations above don&#39;t have intercepts? (JASP doesn&#39;t output intercepts. Can the underlying laavan output intercepts? In JASP, when I selected the option to force the intercepts be zero, then I couldn&#39;t get good R code output using those coefficients either. So I do NOT use intercepts = zero in my model).</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 14px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">The baseline test of the model has a small p-value (9e-29), and the p-values of the regression coefficients are all &lt; 0.05, indeed many are so small that they&#39;re reported in JASP as 0 (and the 95% confidence intervals are good, with no zero within any). All the +- signs of the regression coefficients are as expected. The GFI is 0.969. So I presume the model is good? All be it the CFI is only 0.828, which is a worry?</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px;word-break:break-word;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:rgb(38,50,56);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:16px\">P.S. The data set is quite sparse and I&#39;ve used FIML setting within JASP to populate where there is missing data values. </p>"
